// Merge key = packed tone rgb (+1 so air stays 0): same-tone
// neighbours collapse into one greedy quad while differing tones
// stay separate — crisp per-block pixel grain matching the
// widget's own JS mesher (`game/mesh.js`).
m[vv * su + uu] =
    (((fc[0] * 255).round() << 16) |
        ((fc[1] * 255).round() << 8) |
        (fc[2] * 255).round()) +
    1;
```

The two narratives contradict each other about which merge key is correct; 0.4.177 now attributes the "empty world" chaos to the double origin translation (positions are emitted chunk-local and translated once in `VoxelPainter._collectChunk`). The `apps_voxel_world` golden and the fa_ui test shards pass on 0.4.177, so the current state renders correctly.

